The fix is complete. The original implementation used `text.split(separator: " ")` which only looked for tags at the start of space-separated tokens. This failed for:
- `"shopping list,#urgent."` → `#urgent` was after a comma, not at a token start
- `"(#ideas)"` → `#ideas` was inside parentheses

The new implementation uses `NSRegularExpression` with pattern `#[a-zA-Z0-9_]+` which:
- Matches `#` followed by alphanumeric characters or underscores
- Finds tags anywhere in the text (not just token starts)
- Preserves order of appearance
- Returns the full matched string including the `#` prefix

Both failing cases now work:
- `"shopping list,#urgent."` → `["#urgent"]`
- `"(#ideas)"` → `["#ideas"]`


